    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1083">

                <pb facs="0794" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3908.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-28T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>One of my messengers has just returned with following message from federal
                    General Maas, now at Soledad: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Consul</hi>: I hereby answer your
                            esteemed letter of the 25th instant, advising that in accord with
                            instructions which I have received from my Government the military
                            authorities of the jurisdiction under my command have been ordered to
                            permit foreigners of any nationality whatsoever to leave the Republic at
                            will.</p>
                        <p>Relative to Mexican citizens who desire to leave the city at Vera Cruz
                            you may permit or prohibit same according to the orders you may have in
                            the premises.</p>
                        <p>I am [etc]</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Maas</hi>.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>This communication is dated Soledad de Doblado, April 27.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
